; bookmarks: clean up a bookmarks file that a browser exported, and sort the loose bookmarks.
; Made with "rig.py new", level 4. Code reads the file, removes exact duplicates, groups similar URLs,
; checks every answer and writes the new file. A person chooses in the similar groups, agrees to new
; folders and agrees to the dry-run report. The model only sorts loose bookmarks into folders.
; Language version 1: the lines run in order; "for" runs a page of choices, or a batch to sort, once
; for each item. 18 steps and gates, 4 ends.
; The tool never changes the export or a live file of the browser: it writes a new HTML file to import.

unit bookmarks agent
  intent "clean up a bookmarks HTML file that Edge exported: remove exact duplicates, fold similar URLs as the person chooses, sort loose bookmarks into folders, and write a new file to import"
  in file path "the bookmarks HTML file that Edge exported (Settings, Favorites, Export favorites)"
  out text "the path of the new bookmarks file and of its report"
  code gates gates.py
    test tests/test_gates.py
  code steps steps.py
    test tests/test_steps.py

  rule files.work "work" "Folder for the work of each run"
    note "relative to the tool folder; one sub-folder for each run, with the choices and the sorted batches. Not in version control"
  rule files.out "out" "Folder for the new bookmarks file"
    note "relative to the tool folder; the export stays where it is"
  rule keep.bar on "Leave the favorites bar alone"
    note "a bookmark directly on the favorites bar is a shortcut that the person put there: it is never removed, grouped or moved"
  rule dupes.tracking (utm_ fbclid gclid dclid msclkid mc_cid mc_eid igshid _hsenc _hsmi yclid) "Tracking parameters to ignore"
    note "a name that ends with _ is a prefix. These parameters do not change the page"
  rule similar.skip_hosts (github.com youtube.com youtu.be google.com wikipedia.org stackoverflow.com reddit.com amazon.com medium.com x.com twitter.com facebook.com) "Sites with many separate pages: never group"
    note "on these sites a longer path is another page with its own content, not a variant. Add a site here to stop its groups"
  rule similar.skip_pattern /^(docs|developer|developers|support|help|wiki)\./ "Host names of documentation sites: never group"
  rule similar.index_names (index index.html index.htm index.php home default.aspx default.htm) "Last parts of a path that name the same page as the folder"
    note "home.org/index.html is home.org; code folds such a variant when the short URL is a bookmark too"
  rule similar.max_group 8 "Largest group to show to the person"
    range 2 50
    note "a larger group is a site with many pages, not variants of one page; first value, check it on the real file"
  rule similar.page_size 20 "Groups on one page of choices"
    range 1 100
    note "first value; a page must be easy to read in a chat"
  rule sort.loose_depth 1 "Folders this deep or less hold loose bookmarks"
    range 0 3
    note "1: the top level and the top folders, such as Other favorites. The favorites bar is left alone (keep.bar)"
  rule sort.host_elsewhere 2 "Bookmarks of the same site in another folder that make one likely misfiled"
    range 1 20
    note "first value, set on the test file; a single bookmark of a site in another folder says little"
  rule sort.batch 60 "Bookmarks in one batch for the model"
    range 10 100
    note "the owner asked for batches of about fifty to a hundred; a small local model loses items in a longer list"
  rule sort.rounds 2 "Retries of one batch"
    range 0 5
    note "after the retries the batch stays unsorted and the report lists it"
  rule sort.new_per_batch 3 "New folders in one batch"
    range 0 10
    note "the owner wants the folders of the file plus a few new ones"
  rule sort.new_max 12 "New folders in all"
    range 0 50
    note "the owner wants the folders of the file plus a few new ones"
  rule sort.url_chars 120 "Longest URL that the model sees, in characters"
    range 40 400
    note "a longer URL is cut; the model does not need the query to sort"
  rule sort.title_chars 80 "Longest title that the model and the person see, in characters"
    range 20 300
    note "a longer title is cut in what is shown; the file keeps the whole title"
  rule safety.max_removed 30 "Largest share of bookmarks that one run may remove, in percent"
    range 1 100
    note "a plan that removes more points at a bug or a wrong rule; the run is held back. First value"
  rule links.check off "Check the links (not in this version)"
    note "the hook for a link checker: it will move dead links to the folder links.folder, never delete them"
  rule links.folder "Dead links" "Folder for dead links"
  rule permissions.overwrite off "The tool may write over an earlier new file"
    note "off: when the output file exists, the run ends at held and writes nothing"

  step read "Read the export" by steps.read
    do "read the bookmarks file: every folder with its path, every bookmark with its title, URL, folder and date"
    reads files.work
  gate file-ok hard "A bookmarks export"
    check "the file is a bookmarks file in the Netscape HTML form, with at least one bookmark; the live JSON file of the browser is refused"
    by gates.file_ok
    fail -> bad-file "not a bookmarks export"

  section "Duplicates and similar URLs"
    step similar "Remove exact duplicates, group similar URLs"
      do "find copies of one URL, ignoring http or https, www, a last slash, a #part and the tracking parameters of dupes.tracking; keep the copy in the deeper folder, else the oldest. Then group the URLs of one site where one path starts with another; fold the plain variants of similar.index_names; skip the sites of similar.skip_hosts and similar.skip_pattern; cut the groups into pages"
      by steps.dupes
      by steps.group
      reads dupes.tracking keep.bar similar.index_names similar.skip_hosts similar.skip_pattern similar.max_group similar.page_size
    for page in similar.pages
      step show "Show the page" by steps.page
        do "write the page of groups into a file; when the person said rest on an earlier page, decide this page as they said, and ask nothing"
        reads sort.title_chars
      gate choose human "Which URLs to keep?"
        if show.ask
        options yes | yes rest | no
        check "show the person each group of this page: its site and its URLs with their numbers, and the path of the page file. Give the person the answers of show.how: each one is the end of the command"
        sees show
        by steps.apply
        note "the answer is the words after approve: yes, then G=all, G=short, G=K or rest. no keeps every URL from here on. Code asks again when it does not understand a word"

  section "Sorting"
    step loose "Find loose and misfiled bookmarks" by steps.loose
      do "leave alone the bookmarks that fit their folder; take the loose ones (sort.loose_depth) and the likely misfiled ones (sort.host_elsewhere); cut them into batches of sort.batch"
      reads sort.loose_depth sort.host_elsewhere sort.batch keep.bar
    for batch in loose.batches
      tolerate 20%
      fail -> held "too many batches are left unsorted"
      step prepare "The batch for the model" by steps.prepare
        do "give the bookmarks of the batch and the folder list, with the new folders of the earlier batches"
        reads sort.url_chars sort.title_chars keep.bar
      step sort "Sort the batch" by model
        do "put each bookmark of the batch into the folder where it fits best. Choose a folder of the list folders. A bookmark that fits its present folder keeps that folder. Only when no folder fits, propose a new folder: give its whole path under a folder of the list, and \"new\": true; at most {sort.new_per_batch} new folders in this batch. Give the result as a list with one object for each bookmark: {\"id\": <id>, \"folder\": \"<path>\"}. Write each path as in the list, with > between the names. Do not change a URL or a title. When waiting has problems, your last answer failed: fix them"
        sees prepare
        out (list (record id int folder str new (maybe bool)))
      gate sort-ok hard "Every bookmark once, in a known folder"
        check "the answer has every id of the batch once and no other id, no changed URL or title, only folders of the list or new folders under them, at most {sort.new_per_batch} new folders in the batch and {sort.new_max} in all; then the batch is saved"
        by gates.sort_ok
        by steps.keep
        retry sort.rounds
        fail -> continue "the batch stays unsorted"
        note "steps.keep saves a batch that passed: it runs only after gates.sort_ok passes"
    step folders "Collect the new folders" by steps.folders
      do "list the new folders that the model proposed, with the number of bookmarks and some titles for each"
    gate new-ok human "Make these new folders?"
      if folders.new
      options yes | no
      check "show the person each new folder: its path, how many bookmarks go to it, and the examples. Give the person the answers of folders.how: each one is the end of the command"
      sees folders
      by steps.accept
      note "yes N=no leaves out new folder N: its bookmarks stay where they are. no makes no new folder"

  section "Output"
    step report "Write the dry-run report" by steps.report
      do "count and list what the new file would remove, fold, move and make, and write the report into the work folder; write nothing else. When links.check is on, a later version checks the links first and moves dead ones to links.folder; now it only reads dead.json of the work folder, when it exists"
      reads links.check links.folder
    gate share hard "Not too much removed"
      check "the plan removes at most {safety.max_removed} percent of the bookmarks"
      by gates.share_ok
      fail -> held "the plan removes too much"
    gate approve human "May the tool write the new bookmarks file?"
      check "show the person the counts of the dry run and the path of the report"
      sees report
      fail -> declined "the person said no"
    step build "Build the new file" by steps.build
      do "write the new file into the work folder and read it again"
      reads files.out
    gate verify hard "The new file keeps what it must"
      check "the new file has every bookmark that stays, with its title and URL, every folder of the export with its name, every new folder, and every moved bookmark in its new folder"
      by gates.verify
      fail -> held "the new file failed its check"
    gate target hard "The output file is free"
      reads permissions.overwrite
      check "no file has the name of the output, or the rule permissions.overwrite is on"
      by gates.may_place
      fail -> held "the output file exists"
    step place "Place the new file" by steps.place
      do "copy the checked file to the folder of files.out; the export and the files of the browser stay as they are"
      reads permissions.overwrite
  end done "Written: import the new file into Edge"
  end bad-file "Not a bookmarks export"
  end held "Held back by a safety check: nothing written"
  end declined "The person said no: nothing written"
